{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes","lean:module:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.f_interleaved_ne_f_sequential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.f_interleaved_ne_f_sequential","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FormalityBridgeF1.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**The same statement through `f`.** If `f` is injective on the two traces (in particular for\n`log` on positive reals), the interleaved word's `f`-value differs from the sequential bond sum.\nStated with an explicit injectivity hypothesis rather than a logarithm, per §7c. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.interleaved_ne_sequential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.interleaved_ne_sequential","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FormalityBridgeF1.lean#L90-L102","doc":"**F1, interleaved half.** With a non-zero cross term, the interleaved word `g₀ g₁ g₀ g₂ g₁`\ndoes not have the trace of the sequential word `g₀² g₁² g₂` with the same letter content — so\nits `log` is not that bond sum. The corpus's `n = 4` many-body signal is the failure of F1's\nordering hypothesis, not a counterexample to F1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.f_tr_stabWord_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.f_tr_stabWord_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FormalityBridgeF1.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**F1, sequential half.** For a monotone word of stabilising letters and any map `f` with\n`f (x·y) = f x + f y`, `f (tr word)` is the sum of the letters' `f`-images: `log tr` of a\nsequential word is a bond sum. Combined with\n`MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.b3_eq_zero_of_bondRule`, every connected cumulant above two of\nsuch a binding vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.additive_map_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.additive_map_prod","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FormalityBridgeF1.lean#L68-L75","doc":"A multiplicative-to-additive map turns a finite product into a finite sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.additive_map_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FormalityBridgeF1.additive_map_one","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FormalityBridgeF1.lean#L61-L66","doc":"A multiplicative-to-additive map sends `1` to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}